Acceptance blocker: external driver leaks, not suppressed.
  Default ASan hardware runs fail cuInit with CUDA_ERROR_OUT_OF_MEMORY.
  GPU reported 5172 MiB free during investigation.
  protect_shadow_gap=0 allows CUDA initialization, retaining leak detection.
  ASAN_OPTIONS=detect_leaks=1:protect_shadow_gap=0 ctest --test-dir build-sanitize -L nvidia --output-on-failure
  All 5 hardware tests fail at shutdown on LeakSanitizer reports.
  Leak summaries: nvenc 279 bytes/6 allocations, nvdec 231/5, nvidia-roundtrip 279/6.
  Subprocess tests also fail on the encoder's 279-byte leak report.
  No other ASan or UBSan diagnostic appeared in this run.

Independent CUDA probe, no FFmpeg or L.A.R.P. codec code linked:
  ASAN_OPTIONS=detect_leaks=1:protect_shadow_gap=0 build-sanitize/larp-cuda-init
  cuInit: 0
  SUMMARY: AddressSanitizer: 183 byte(s) leaked in 4 allocation(s).
  Direct allocation stack: calloc -> libcuda.so.1+0x30caea -> cuInit.
  A standalone experiment creating and destroying ten CUDA contexts gave the same
  183-byte baseline. RTLD_NODELETE did not remove it; no such workaround was added.

